{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.archimedean_realize_pointwise_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.archimedean_realize_pointwise_unique","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L53-L68","doc":"**Pointwise uniqueness companion.**  Two `ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor`\ninstances on a *common* `Motive` type that share the same\n`eulerChar` and `archimedeanProjection` agree on every motive.\n\nThe proof rewrites both sides via `archimedean_realize_determined`\nto the common `projection ∘ Int.cast ∘ eulerChar` expression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.archimedean_realize_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.archimedean_realize_determined","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L34-L51","doc":"**Determination theorem (uniqueness backbone).**\n\nThe `realize` function of any `ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor` is\nfully determined by its `eulerChar` and `archimedeanProjection`\nfields via the `compat_integer` compatibility law.  Hence two\nrealisations with identical `eulerChar` and identical\n`archimedeanProjection` on the same `Motive` type produce\nidentical `realize` outputs — the structural backbone of the\nArchimedean realisation uniqueness theorem (uniqueness-theorems-\nbacklog.md item 5).\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: structural uniqueness immediate from the\n`compat_integer` axiom carried by the structure itself; no\nadditional class needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.compat_integer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.compat_integer","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Compatibility: R_top = π_∞ ∘ (ℤ → ℝ) ∘ χ_top on integer-valued motives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.realize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.realize","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Real-valued realization R_top : Motive → ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.archimedeanProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.archimedeanProjection","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Archimedean projection π_∞ : 𝔸 → ℝ on the adelic ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L26-L26","doc":"Topological Euler characteristic χ_top : M̂ → ℤ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.Motive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.Motive","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L24-L24","doc":"Source: the dimension-completion M̂ of the Grothendieck ring (carrier). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor","kind":"structure","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.lean#L14-L32","doc":"The **archimedean realization functor** R_top.\n\nComposite of the topological realization (motivic class →\ninteger Euler characteristic, or refined Hodge invariant) and\nthe archimedean projection π_∞ : 𝔸 → ℝ of the adelic substrate.\n\nMaps a motivic mass μ(X) ∈ M̂ to a real-valued physical\nobservable Obs_ℝ(X) = R_top(∫ dμ). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:archimedean-realization-functor","label":"def:archimedean-realization-functor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}